SPECIAL NOTES

For the purposes of the above spells, Undead are divided into 6 classes: I, II, III, IV, V, and above V. A GM must place each of the Undead types in his world systems into one of these classes for the purposes of these spells. For example, Skel- etons would obviously be Class I Undead, Mummies might be Class IV or V, Vampires would be above Class V, etc. See Creatures & Monsters for a complete classification of various Undead. Animated Dead are normally treated as Class I Undead. Also note that Undead do not normally get RRs versus spells from the Necromancy list. See Section 7.2.2 for notes on Undead. See Section 7.3 for more information on using Evil spell lists.
